body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

In `preAttemptNoMsAssetRefs`, if the `pre_attempt_blocked` fixture is missing (i.e., `preAttempt` is `undefined`), the function will return `true` because `numberFrom(undefined)` evaluates to `0` and `asArray(undefined).length` is `0`. This results in a silent fail-open bug where the check passes even if the required fixture is absent. Explicitly verify that `preAttempt` is defined before performing checks.

```suggestion
function preAttemptNoMsAssetRefs(fixtures, closeout) {
  const preAttempt = asArray(fixtures?.fixtures).find((fixture) => fixture.fixture_id === 'pre_attempt_blocked');
  if (!preAttempt) return false;
  const controlledRefs = asArray(preAttempt?.source_view?.controlled_asset_refs);
  return numberFrom(preAttempt?.initial_payload?.ms_asset_ref_count) === 0
    && controlledRefs.length === 0
    && numberFrom(closeout?.final_counts?.pre_attempt_network_request_count) === 0
    && numberFrom(closeout?.final_counts?.initial_payload_static_props_bundle_ms_asset_ref_count) === 0;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Validation functions for fixtures should fail closed with a specific error code (e.g., 'fixture_record_required') for malformed fixture records and validate objective references instead of allowing null references through.
</details>

