body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The current implementation of `requiredFixtureIdsPresent` uses `.join('|')` to compare the mapped fixture IDs against `REQUIRED_FIXTURE_IDS.join('|')`. This is strictly order-sensitive and fragile. Explicitly verify the presence of each expected element using a set-based check to ensure robust validation.

```suggestion
function requiredFixtureIdsPresent(fixtures) {
  const presentIds = new Set(asArray(fixtures?.fixtures).map((fixture) => fixture?.fixture_id));
  return REQUIRED_FIXTURE_IDS.every((id) => presentIds.has(id))
    && presentIds.size === REQUIRED_FIXTURE_IDS.length;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When validating that an array contains a complete set of expected elements, explicitly verify the presence and state of each expected element rather than filtering and checking only the elements present in the array. Accompany this with regression tests that omit expected elements to ensure the validation fails closed.
</details>

